  "notes": "Official cause code is TBD/provisional per FORM-366 fields; narrative describes direct cause (charging motor loose, bushing failed, wires severed) and contributing cause (inadequate procedure guidance for tightening charging motor). Modeled bushing failure and wire severance as two parallel failure modes both stemming from the loose motor and both feeding into inability to charge springs, per rule 5. Past operability review determined failure likely occurred on 2024-02-18 (last successful close) though discovered 2024-04-10; used the 2024-02-18 to 2024-04-11 window per the ~50-day inoperability duration stated in the narrative. No previous similar event was referenced in the narrative (section present but empty), so no SIMILAR_TO/stub LER emitted per rule 9's conditional applicability. USST/SSST transformers and general 4KV bus description are background/design context, not directly involved in the failure chain, so not modeled as separate System/Component nodes beyond EA/EB umbrella systems and the specific breaker involved."
